#N canvas 0 50 1040 1300 12;
#X text 30 16 =^..^=   ms20~   version 1 (2026)   sofia vallejo budziszewski   iem kug graz austria;
#X text 30 46 ms-20 style monosynth with patch matrix;
#X text 30 86 two oscillators with ring modulation and noise feed a high-pass and a low-pass filter that scream when you raise the peak. two envelope generators and a modulation generator are wired by a matrix of amounts: every source can go to pitch pulse width and both cutoffs. mono., f 110;
#X text 30 166 --- how it was made ---;
#X text 30 210 the two filters are two-pole state variable filters with a soft-clipped band state. at the top of the peak control the damping goes slightly negative so they oscillate by themselves., f 110;
#X text 30 260 there are no cables. the patch panel is a matrix of amounts (0.5 is off) so every source can reach every destination., f 110;
#X text 30 310 oscillator 1 and 2 can be multiplied by the ring control. the high-pass and low-pass run in series or in parallel., f 110;
#X text 30 370 --- how to use ---;
#X text 30 414 1  open the engine page below and turn dsp on, f 110;
#X text 30 444 2  play a midi keyboard or click chord on, f 110;
#X text 30 474 3  open the parameters page and move any control or open presets and step through the sounds, f 110;
#X text 30 504 4  everything is a message: see the messages page for the full list and the examples page for patches to copy, f 110;
#X text 30 564 try:  load screamer and raise lppeak to the top: the low-pass oscillates and plays pitch with the keys, f 110;
#X text 30 594 try:  move mg2lp and mg2hp in opposite directions: the two filters sweep against each other, f 110;
#X text 30 624 try:  raise ring with two different tunes for bells and metallic hits, f 110;
#X text 30 668 --- common problems ---;
#X text 30 712 no sound: turn dsp on in the engine page and check the volume slider. the synth needs a note: click chord on or play a midi key, f 110;
#X text 30 762 nothing changes after a rebuild: pd keeps the old external in memory so close every patch and restart pd, f 110;
#X text 30 792 a note is stuck: send panic. a missing note off from a midi device is the usual cause, f 110;
#X text 30 822 unknown parameter in the console: names are exact and lowercase so send params to print them all, f 110;
#X text 30 852 a bank file is not found: save and load names are relative to the folder of this patch, f 110;
#X text 30 882 the sliders do not move when you change a preset: the object must be created with the same name as in the boxes. default name is the object name, f 110;
#X text 30 932 clicks or dropouts: raise the audio buffer in the pd audio settings or lower the voice count in the creation argument, f 110;
#X text 30 982 a filter screams too loud: lower drive or the peak of that filter, f 110;
#X text 30 1012 no sound at all: check lvl1 lvl2 ring and noise since any of them can be zero, f 110;
#X text 30 1056 --- click a box to open that page ---;
#N canvas 0 50 900 1008 presets 0;
#X text 30 16 presets: factory sounds are stored as plain text and every control above is a message. click a box to load that sound, f 100;
#X text 30 66 --- factory presets ---;
#X msg 30 110 \; ms20 preset 0;
#X text 250 112 0  screamer;
#X msg 30 144 \; ms20 preset 1;
#X text 250 146 1  ring bell;
#X msg 30 178 \; ms20 preset 2;
#X text 250 180 2  wow bass;
#X msg 30 212 \; ms20 preset 3;
#X text 250 214 3  sync alarm;
#X msg 30 246 \; ms20 preset 4;
#X text 250 248 4  filter wah;
#X msg 30 280 \; ms20 preset 5;
#X text 250 282 5  pulse lead;
#X msg 460 110 \; ms20 preset 6;
#X text 680 112 6  wind noise;
#X msg 460 144 \; ms20 preset 7;
#X text 680 146 7  zap pitch;
#X msg 460 178 \; ms20 preset 8;
#X text 680 180 8  dual saw;
#X msg 460 212 \; ms20 preset 9;
#X text 680 214 9  sub growl;
#X msg 460 246 \; ms20 preset 10;
#X text 680 248 10  self sine;
#X msg 460 280 \; ms20 preset 11;
#X text 680 282 11  tri flute;
#X text 30 334 --- now playing ---;
#X symbolatom 30 378 20 0 0 0 - ms20-name - 0;
#X floatatom 230 378 4 0 0 0 - ms20-index - 0;
#X text 340 380 name and number (minus one means edited);
#X msg 30 422 \; ms20 next;
#X msg 158 422 \; ms20 prev;
#X msg 286 422 \; ms20 mutate 0.3;
#X text 30 462 next and prev step through the presets and wrap around. mutate varies the current sound by a random amount from 0 to 1, f 100;
#X text 30 512 --- morph between two sounds ---;
#X msg 30 556 \; ms20 A;
#X msg 134 556 \; ms20 B;
#X text 238 558 a and b remember the current sound;
#X text 30 598 morph;
#X obj 110 596 hsl 300 18 0 1 0 0 ms20-morph ms20-morph-r empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 30 640 load one preset and press a then load another and press b then move the morph slider. every parameter blends smoothly between the two, f 100;
#X text 30 690 --- your own user bank ---;
#X msg 30 734 \; ms20 store mysound;
#X msg 230 734 \; ms20 save my.bank;
#X msg 422 734 \; ms20 load my.bank;
#X text 30 774 store keeps the current sound after the factory presets. save writes the user bank to a text file next to this patch and load adds the sounds from a text file, f 100;
#X text 30 824 --- presets with stash ---;
#X text 30 868 every slider in the parameters page sends to ms20-name and listens on ms20-name-r so the stash library can store and morph whole scenes: create [stash/bank ms20] and send it a scan message for a saved copy of the parameters page. this follows the stash naming rules but has not been tested together yet, f 100;
#X restore 30 1100 pd presets;
#X text 30 1134 all sounds and morph, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1500 2028 parameters 0;
#X text 30 16 every control here is also a message: set name value with values from 0 to 1. switches take the step number shown under each one, f 120;
